ADR-112 Secure Baseline Posture
===============================
5 deviation(s) found (4 from shipped defaults, 1 explicitly configured) — all counted:
  [insecure-setting/shipped-default] security.insecure_skip_startup_validation is in effect (grace-warn-only) — NEEDS ANDREI (polarity-inverted rename of security.enable_file_permission_check, which item 1 just gave ADR-112 default-flip + grace-period machinery under its current name) -- the file-permission/DEK-salt-size/database-reachability startup checks are skipped (off) or, in the ADR-112 upgrade grace period (grace-warn-only), only warn instead of refusing to start
  [insecure-setting/explicit] storage.encryption.insecure_disable_encryption_at_rest is in effect (true) — NEEDS ANDREI (polarity-inverted rename of storage.encryption.enabled, a high-blast-radius architectural flag, not purely a weakening toggle) -- secrets stored unencrypted at rest
  [insecure-setting/shipped-default] server.insecure_allow_unauthenticated_metrics is in effect (true) — NEEDS ANDREI (not a boolean today -- an empty server.http/grpc.metrics_token string) -- /metrics served fully unauthenticated
  [insecure-setting/shipped-default] server.insecure_disable_api_ratelimit is in effect (true) — NEEDS ANDREI (polarity-inverted rename, AND already ships disabled by default -- the same inverted-default shape item 1 fixed for two other settings; this one needs the same product decision) -- removes per-principal API rate limiting
  [grace-period/shipped-default] security.enable_file_permission_check is in its ADR-112 upgrade grace period: this upgraded deployment never set it, so a failed startup check only WARNS and the server starts anyway. Fix anything the startup checks report; the first clean boot then ends the grace period for good (adr112.file_permission_check.enforced), or set security.enable_file_permission_check: true explicitly
